---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="API — PURSUE://INDEX"
  description="Programmatic access to the pursueindex corpus: /api/retrieve for semantic search and /api/chat for streaming RAG. CORS-locked to pursueindex.com but reachable from non-browser clients (curl, scripts)."
>
  <article class="space-y-8 max-w-3xl">
    <header class="space-y-2 border-b border-[color:var(--color-border)] pb-4">
      <div class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[color:var(--color-signal-green)] flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="text-[color:var(--color-text-faint)]">$</span>
        <span>man pursue-index --section api</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-2xl font-mono font-semibold tracking-tight text-[color:var(--color-text-bright)]">
        API
      </h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-[color:var(--color-text-dim)] max-w-2xl">
        Programmatic access to the pursueindex corpus for researchers,
        journalists, and tinkerers. Two endpoints — semantic search and
        streaming RAG — both read-only, both reachable from non-browser
        clients. Anonymous tier is rate-limited to keep the lights on; for
        higher-volume use, bring your own Anthropic key.
      </p>
    </header>

    {/* 1. Surface overview */}
    <section id="surface" class="border border-[color:var(--color-border)] bg-[color:var(--color-bg)]/60 p-5 pi-bracket relative scanlines-soft space-y-3 scroll-mt-20">
      <h2 class="font-mono text-[12px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[color:var(--color-signal-green)]">
        ▸ Surface overview
      </h2>
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--color-text)]">
        Two endpoints, both <code class="text-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)]">POST</code> with
        a JSON body, both anonymous (no auth header). All requests are
        read-only; nothing on the corpus or the index can be mutated through
        this surface.
      </p>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="w-full text-xs font-mono border-collapse">
          <thead>
            <tr class="border-b border-[color:var(--color-border-bright)] text-[color:var(--color-text-faint)] uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-[10px]">
              <th class="text-left py-2 pr-4">Endpoint</th>
              <th class="text-left py-2 pr-4">Purpose</th>
              <th class="text-left py-2 pr-4">Response</th>
              <th class="text-left py-2">Rate limit</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="text-[color:var(--color-text)]">
            <tr class="border-b border-[color:var(--color-border)]">
              <td class="py-2 pr-4 text-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)]">POST /api/retrieve</td>
              <td class="py-2 pr-4">Voyage-3 semantic search</td>
              <td class="py-2 pr-4">JSON</td>
              <td class="py-2 text-[color:var(--color-text-dim)]">Uncapped (read-only, ~free)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="py-2 pr-4 text-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)]">POST /api/chat</td>
              <td class="py-2 pr-4">Streaming RAG (Sonnet 4.6)</td>
              <td class="py-2 pr-4">SSE</td>
              <td class="py-2 text-[color:var(--color-text-dim)]">5 chats / IP / 24h</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--color-text)]">
        <strong class="text-[color:var(--color-text-bright)]">CORS posture.</strong>
        The Worker locks <code class="text-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)]">/api/*</code>
        to <code class="text-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)]">https://pursueindex.com</code>
        and <code class="text-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)]">https://www.pursueindex.com</code>;
        browser fetches from any other origin get a 403. Programmatic
        clients — curl, server-side scripts, language SDKs (Python, Go,
        Node, etc.) — are supported. Anonymous-tier abuse is bounded by
        the per-IP rate limit on <code>/api/chat</code>.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--color-text)]">
        <strong class="text-[color:var(--color-text-bright)]">BYOK.</strong>
        For chat traffic above the anonymous cap, paste an Anthropic key
        into the <a href="/chat" class="text-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)] underline decoration-[color:var(--color-border-bright)] hover:decoration-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)]">Settings</a>
        panel on <code>/chat</code>. The browser then calls Anthropic
        directly with the
        <code class="text-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)]">anthropic-dangerous-direct-browser-access: true</code>
        header — your key never touches our Worker. Programmatic BYOK is
        not supported via this Worker; the Worker is anonymous-tier only.
        If you need scripted high-volume access, call Anthropic yourself
        and use <code>/api/retrieve</code> for the retrieval step.
      </p>
    </section>

    {/* 2. /api/retrieve */}
    <section id="retrieve" class="border border-[color:var(--color-border)] bg-[color:var(--color-bg)]/60 p-5 space-y-3 scroll-mt-20">
      <h2 class="font-mono text-[12px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[color:var(--color-signal-green)]">
        ▸ POST /api/retrieve — semantic search
      </h2>
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--color-text)]">
        Embeds your query with <code class="text-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)]">voyage-3</code>
        and returns the top-k passages by cosine similarity over the
        shipped augmented embeddings. No rate limit on this endpoint —
        retrieval is essentially free, so we let researchers pull as much
        as they want. Results below cosine
        <code class="text-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)]">0.30</code>
        are filtered out.
      </p>
      <p class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-[color:var(--color-text-faint)]">Request</p>
      <pre class="bg-[color:var(--color-bg-elevated)] border border-[color:var(--color-border)] p-3 font-mono text-[11px] text-[color:var(--color-text-bright)] overflow-x-auto whitespace-pre"><code>{`POST /api/retrieve
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "Apollo 17 anomalies during EVA",
  "k": 8
}`}</code></pre>
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--color-text)]">
        <code class="text-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)]">k</code> is
        optional (default 8, min 1, max 20). <code>query</code> is
        required, max 1000 chars.
      </p>
      <p class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-[color:var(--color-text-faint)]">Response</p>
      <pre class="bg-[color:var(--color-bg-elevated)] border border-[color:var(--color-border)] p-3 font-mono text-[11px] text-[color:var(--color-text-bright)] overflow-x-auto whitespace-pre"><code>{`{
  "passages": [
    {
      "card_id": "0b298cfc9c65a4d6",
      "page": 17,
      "title": "NASA-UAP-D6, Apollo 17 Technical Crew Debriefing, 1973",
      "snippet": "…unidentified flash on the lunar surface…",
      "score": 0.6421,
      "page_text": "<full page OCR text>"
    }
  ],
  "model": "voyage-3",
  "k": 8,
  "threshold": 0.3
}`}</code></pre>
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--color-text)]">
        <code class="text-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)]">snippet</code>
        is a query-centered ~600-char window; <code>page_text</code> is
        the full page OCR (handy if you're feeding this into your own
        RAG). <code>card_id</code> + <code>page</code> resolve to
        <code class="text-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)]">https://pursueindex.com/card/&lt;card_id&gt;#page-&lt;n&gt;</code>.
      </p>
      <p class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-[color:var(--color-text-faint)]">curl</p>
      <pre class="bg-[color:var(--color-bg-elevated)] border border-[color:var(--color-border)] p-3 font-mono text-[11px] text-[color:var(--color-text-bright)] overflow-x-auto whitespace-pre"><code>{`curl -s -X POST https://pursueindex.com/api/retrieve \\
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \\
  -d '{"query":"Apollo 17 anomalies during EVA","k":5}'`}</code></pre>
    </section>

    {/* 3. /api/chat */}
    <section id="chat" class="border border-[color:var(--color-border)] bg-[color:var(--color-bg)]/60 p-5 space-y-3 scroll-mt-20">
      <h2 class="font-mono text-[12px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[color:var(--color-signal-green)]">
        ▸ POST /api/chat — streaming RAG
      </h2>
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--color-text)]">
        Retrieves top-8 passages, hands them to Anthropic's
        <code class="text-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)]">claude-sonnet-4-6</code>
        with a system prompt that enforces inline
        <code class="text-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)]">[card_id:page]</code>
        citations and abstention on off-corpus questions, and streams the
        response back as Server-Sent Events. The exact model may be
        updated as Anthropic releases new generations; the canonical
        value lives in <code>worker/chat.js</code>
        (<code>DEFAULT_MODEL</code>) and the page is regenerated when it
        changes.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--color-text)]">
        <strong class="text-[color:var(--color-text-bright)]">Anonymous tier limits.</strong>
        5 chats per IP per UTC day. Global daily spend cap of $100 USD
        across all callers; once that's hit, the endpoint returns 503
        until the next UTC day rolls over. A 24-hour semantic cache means
        repeated identical queries replay without burning rate budget or
        spend. Off-corpus questions skip Anthropic entirely and stream a
        canned abstention — also free, also no rate counter increment.
      </p>
      <p class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-[color:var(--color-text-faint)]">Request</p>
      <pre class="bg-[color:var(--color-bg-elevated)] border border-[color:var(--color-border)] p-3 font-mono text-[11px] text-[color:var(--color-text-bright)] overflow-x-auto whitespace-pre"><code>{`POST /api/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "What did the FBI 62-HQ-83894 file say about Roswell?"
}`}</code></pre>
      <p class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-[color:var(--color-text-faint)]">Response — SSE wire format</p>
      <pre class="bg-[color:var(--color-bg-elevated)] border border-[color:var(--color-border)] p-3 font-mono text-[11px] text-[color:var(--color-text-bright)] overflow-x-auto whitespace-pre"><code>{`event: citations
data: [{"card_id":"a1b2c3d4e5f6","page":5,"title":"...","snippet":"…","score":0.71}, …]

event: text
data: {"delta":"The 62-HQ-83894 file"}

event: text
data: {"delta":" contains a 1950 memo"}

…

event: done
data: {"usage":{"input_tokens":1234,"output_tokens":456}}`}</code></pre>
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--color-text)]">
        <code>citations</code> arrives first with the retrieved passages,
        then a stream of <code>text</code> deltas, then <code>done</code>
        with the usage stats. Mid-stream failures emit
        <code class="text-[color:var(--color-signal-amber)]">event: error</code>
        with a sanitized message before the stream closes — your client
        should handle that as a terminal event.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--color-text)]">
        <strong class="text-[color:var(--color-text-bright)]">Optional flags on <code>done</code>.</strong>
        Cache replays add <code class="text-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)]">cached: true</code>;
        canned abstentions (off-corpus retrieval) add
        <code class="text-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)]">abstained: true</code>.
        Both are additive — the
        <code>usage</code> field is always present, the flags appear only
        when relevant. Neither replays a fresh Anthropic call, so neither
        increments the per-IP rate counter or contributes to the daily
        spend cap.
      </p>
      <p class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-[color:var(--color-text-faint)]">curl — consume the SSE stream</p>
      <pre class="bg-[color:var(--color-bg-elevated)] border border-[color:var(--color-border)] p-3 font-mono text-[11px] text-[color:var(--color-text-bright)] overflow-x-auto whitespace-pre"><code>{`curl -N -X POST https://pursueindex.com/api/chat \\
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \\
  -d '{"query":"What did the FBI 62-HQ-83894 file say about Roswell?"}'`}</code></pre>
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--color-text)]">
        <code>-N</code> disables curl's output buffering so you see the
        deltas as they arrive. Without it, curl may hold the response
        until the stream closes and you lose the streaming behavior.
      </p>
    </section>

    {/* 4. Citation contract */}
    <section id="citations" class="border border-[color:var(--color-border)] bg-[color:var(--color-bg)]/60 p-5 space-y-3 scroll-mt-20">
      <h2 class="font-mono text-[12px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[color:var(--color-signal-green)]">
        ▸ Citation contract
      </h2>
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--color-text)]">
        Every factual claim in <code>/api/chat</code> output ends with a
        <code class="text-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)]">[card_id:page]</code>
        marker. Multiple citations per claim are encouraged. The system
        prompt enforces this as Rule 2 (cite the source of each individual
        claim, not just the end of the answer) and Rule 3 (abstain on
        off-corpus questions rather than draw on training data).
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--color-text)]">
        Clients can parse these markers with a trivial regex —
        <code class="text-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)]">/\[([0-9a-f]{`{16}`}):(\d+)\]/g</code> —
        and resolve each match to a primary source. The page anchor is a
        hash fragment; the card detail page handles the scroll:
      </p>
      <pre class="bg-[color:var(--color-bg-elevated)] border border-[color:var(--color-border)] p-3 font-mono text-[11px] text-[color:var(--color-text-bright)] overflow-x-auto whitespace-pre"><code>{`https://pursueindex.com/card/<card_id>#page-<n>`}</code></pre>
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--color-text)]">
        See <a href="/cite" class="text-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)] underline decoration-[color:var(--color-border-bright)] hover:decoration-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)]">/cite</a>
        for citation forms when you publish — the
        <code>card_id</code> is stable across re-fetches because it's
        <code class="text-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)]">sha256(asset_url || title)[:16]</code>.
        Disclosing the derivation is fine here because the corpus is
        public-domain U.S. Government work; if any deployment of this
        codebase indexes private or restricted documents, this paragraph
        must be removed before going live (see
        <a href="https://github.com/BPSAI/pursue-index/blob/main/SECURITY.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="text-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)] underline decoration-[color:var(--color-border-bright)] hover:decoration-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)]">SECURITY.md</a>).
      </p>
    </section>

    {/* 5. Errors */}
    <section id="errors" class="border border-[color:var(--color-border)] bg-[color:var(--color-bg)]/60 p-5 space-y-3 scroll-mt-20">
      <h2 class="font-mono text-[12px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[color:var(--color-signal-green)]">
        ▸ Errors and behavior
      </h2>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="w-full text-xs font-mono border-collapse">
          <thead>
            <tr class="border-b border-[color:var(--color-border-bright)] text-[color:var(--color-text-faint)] uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-[10px]">
              <th class="text-left py-2 pr-4">Status</th>
              <th class="text-left py-2 pr-4">When</th>
              <th class="text-left py-2">Body</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="text-[color:var(--color-text)]">
            <tr class="border-b border-[color:var(--color-border)]">
              <td class="py-2 pr-4 text-[color:var(--color-signal-amber)]">400</td>
              <td class="py-2 pr-4">Missing/empty <code>query</code>, malformed JSON, or query &gt;1000 chars</td>
              <td class="py-2 text-[color:var(--color-text-dim)]"><code>{`{"error":"…"}`}</code></td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-[color:var(--color-border)]">
              <td class="py-2 pr-4 text-[color:var(--color-signal-amber)]">403</td>
              <td class="py-2 pr-4">Browser sending <code>Origin</code> header that isn't in the allowlist</td>
              <td class="py-2 text-[color:var(--color-text-dim)]"><code>{`{"error":"cross-origin not allowed"}`}</code></td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-[color:var(--color-border)]">
              <td class="py-2 pr-4 text-[color:var(--color-signal-amber)]">405</td>
              <td class="py-2 pr-4">Non-POST request to <code>/api/chat</code> or <code>/api/retrieve</code> (method not allowed)</td>
              <td class="py-2 text-[color:var(--color-text-dim)]"><code>{`{"error":"method not allowed"}`}</code></td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-[color:var(--color-border)]">
              <td class="py-2 pr-4 text-[color:var(--color-signal-amber)]">429</td>
              <td class="py-2 pr-4">Per-IP daily rate limit exceeded (chat only — 5 / IP / 24h)</td>
              <td class="py-2 text-[color:var(--color-text-dim)]"><code>{`{"error":"…BYOK…","rate_limit":N}`}</code></td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-[color:var(--color-border)]">
              <td class="py-2 pr-4 text-[color:var(--color-signal-amber)]">502</td>
              <td class="py-2 pr-4">Upstream Voyage embed failure</td>
              <td class="py-2 text-[color:var(--color-text-dim)]"><code>{`{"error":"…"}`}</code></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="py-2 pr-4 text-[color:var(--color-signal-amber)]">503</td>
              <td class="py-2 pr-4">Daily $100 global budget cap reached (chat only)</td>
              <td class="py-2 text-[color:var(--color-text-dim)]"><code>{`{"error":"…try BYOK…"}`}</code></td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--color-text)]">
        <strong class="text-[color:var(--color-text-bright)]">429 body shape.</strong>
        <code>rate_limit</code> is the <strong>current count</strong> for
        the calling IP at the moment the request was refused (not the
        cap, not a remaining quota). The cap itself is fixed — 5 chats
        per IP per UTC day — so a backoff client can compare against
        that constant locally. The Worker does <em>not</em> emit a
        <code>Retry-After</code> header today; clients should retry no
        sooner than the next UTC midnight, when the per-IP counter rolls
        over to a new date bucket.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--color-text)]">
        Errors that happen <em>during</em> an SSE stream — e.g., Anthropic
        429s after the citations frame has already gone out — arrive as
        <code class="text-[color:var(--color-signal-amber)]">event: error</code>
        with a sanitized message and an upstream status code, not as an
        HTTP error. The HTTP response itself was already 200 by the time
        the stream opened.
      </p>
    </section>

    {/* 6. Disclaimer + license */}
    <section id="license" class="border border-[color:var(--color-border)] bg-[color:var(--color-bg)]/60 p-5 space-y-3 scroll-mt-20">
      <h2 class="font-mono text-[12px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[color:var(--color-signal-green)]">
        ▸ Disclaimer and license
      </h2>
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--color-text)]">
        API access is offered as a courtesy to researchers, journalists,
        and tinkerers. Both endpoints are read-only — there are no
        destructive operations to worry about — but the rate limit and
        the daily spend cap exist because someone is paying the bill on
        the anonymous tier. For higher-volume use,
        <a href="/chat" class="text-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)] underline decoration-[color:var(--color-border-bright)] hover:decoration-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)]"> BYOK</a>
        is the intended path. Please don't try to launder anonymous-tier
        traffic through proxy IPs to dodge the cap; we'd rather you ask.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--color-text)]">
        Source documents are works of the U.S. Government and in the
        public domain. The OCR transcripts derived from them carry no
        additional copyright claim from us. Index code and this site are
        <a href="https://bpsaisoftware.com" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="text-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)] underline decoration-[color:var(--color-border-bright)] hover:decoration-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)]"> © BPS AI Software</a>,
        licensed under the
        <a href="https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="text-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)] underline decoration-[color:var(--color-border-bright)] hover:decoration-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)]"> Apache License, Version 2.0</a>.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--color-text)]">
        For citation guidance when published research uses retrieved
        snippets — corpus-level, page-level, OCR-transcript, or
        image-description forms — see
        <a href="/cite" class="text-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)] underline decoration-[color:var(--color-border-bright)] hover:decoration-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)]">/cite</a>.
        Methodology and engine numbers live at
        <a href="/methodology" class="text-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)] underline decoration-[color:var(--color-border-bright)] hover:decoration-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)]">/methodology</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <p class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-[color:var(--color-text-faint)] pt-2">
      DOC · <span class="text-[color:var(--color-signal-amber)]">RESEARCH PREVIEW</span>
      <span class="mx-2">·</span>
      REV · <span class="text-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)]">0.1</span>
      <span class="mx-2">·</span>
      SURFACE · <span class="text-[color:var(--color-signal-cyan)]">/api/retrieve · /api/chat</span>
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
